# Byte-identical checkouts on every platform. This is not a style preference.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. Two artefacts in this repo are hashed over RAW BYTES and break silently
# when that happens:
#
#   1. scripts/freeze_aut.py records sha256 of every aut-*/corpus/* file, so that the
#      freeze answers "which policy text was frozen in", not just "which code". Under a
#      CRLF checkout the worked example goes 4627 -> 4686 bytes and
#      8deeef5a99cf5d84... -> f3e99a2f7164eb86..., so a reviewer verifying commitment C3
#      against a fresh clone finds a mismatch and concludes the corpus was tampered with.
#      A verification step that raises false alarms is worse than no verification step.
#
#   2. DESIGN.md 7.1 ships "URLs, fetch timestamps, content hashes and the fetcher" so a
#      third party can check the policy corpus without us redistributing it. Those hashes
#      have to be reproducible from a clone with sha256sum or Get-FileHash.
#
# The harness ingest path is already immune and does not need this: Path.read_text() does
# universal-newline translation, segmenter.py splits with splitlines(), and normalize()
# ends in " ".join(text.split()), which discards \r. So what follows protects the
# raw-byte artefacts, not the clause hashes.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out as well as covered by the wildcard, so that editing the line above cannot
# quietly un-pin the file types whose bytes are load-bearing.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
